This problem can be solved using 3 approaches
BRUTE FORCE APPROACH : Nested loops
BETTER APPROACH : prefix/suffix
OPTIMAL APPROACH : Two Pointers

Core pattern:
---------------
For each index i
  ↓
Find left_max and right_max
  ↓
water = min(left_max, right_max) - height[i]
  ↓
total = total + water
  ↓
Repeat for all indices
  ↓
Print total

BRUTE FORCE APPROACH:
------------------------------

n = list(map(int, input().split()))
total = 0
for i in range(len(n)):
    left_max = 0
    right_max = 0
    for j in range(i + 1):
        left_max = max(left_max, n[j])
    for j in range(i, len(n)):
        right_max = max(right_max, n[j])
    water = min(left_max, right_max) - n[i]
    if water > 0:
        total += water
print(total)

TC:O(n²)
SC:O(1)


BETTER APPROACH:
---------------------------------------
n=list(map(int,input().split()))
size=len(n)
left_max=[0]*size
right_max=[0]*size
#Build prefix
left_max[0]=n[0]
for i in range(1,size):
  left_max[i]=max(left_max[i-1],n[i])
#Build suffix
right_max[-1]=n[-1]
for i in range(size-2,-1,-1):
  right_max[i]=max(right_max[i+1],n[i])
#caluclate trapped_water
total=0
for i in range(size):
  water_level=min(left_max[i],right_max[i])-n[i]
  total+=water_level
print(total)

TC:O(n)--> we traverse the array a constant number of times.
SC:O(n)--> we store two additional arrays whose sizes depend on the input length.

OPTIMAL APPROACH:
----------------------------------------

n = list(map(int, input().split()))
i = 0
j = len(n) - 1
left_max = 0
right_max = 0
total = 0
while i < j:
    if n[i] <= n[j]:
        if n[i] > left_max:
            left_max = n[i]
        else:
            total += left_max - n[i]
        i += 1
    else:
        if n[j] > right_max:
            right_max = n[j]
        else:
            total += right_max - n[j]
        j -= 1
print(total)

TC:O(n)
SC:O(1)



